<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ZCI keeps interim share steady.</title>
<headline>ZCI keeps interim share steady.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million U.S. dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)     0.30	 vs     0.32</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     0.37	 vs     0.39</p>
<p>    Admin costs		 0.32	 vs     0.29</p>
<p>Interest and other</p>
<p>    financial income	  0.97	 vs     0.94</p>
<p>Share of Konkola project</p>
<p>    consortium expenses     0.18	 vs     0.26</p>
<p>Full name: Zambia Copper Investments Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the process of privatising Zambia Consolidated Copper Mines Ltd was underway. The first stage, to be completed in the second half of 1997, would involve the sale by ZCCM of substantial majority stakes of its operating and developing assets in separate packages.</p>
<p>The second stage, expected to follow in the first half of 1998, would involve the disposal by the Zambian goverment of all or a substantial part of its stake in ZCCM to the public and financial institutions.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
